+# Shared workflow contracts pilot
+
+This source-only preparatory owner contains the existing immutable-diagnostic
+sink/trial and application context, plus a three-operation exact-recovery port.
+It owns no numerical algorithm, loader, network client, journal, file lock,
+checkpoint counter, cancellation policy, or publication implementation.
+
+`RoomOptimizationResult` already belongs to the engine and stays there.
+`PipelineObserver` also stays in the engine; no second observer is introduced.
+The application keeps its concrete `RoomRecoverySession` and forwards the port
+operations to its unchanged methods. Snapshot identity checks and the existing
+checkpoint durability callback stay in that concrete implementation. Stage and
+output publication transitions remain application-owned.
+
+The workflow's old public diagnostic/context paths reexport these same items.
+Only internal recovery borrows change to the port. The application pipeline
+still owns the concrete session and passes it to numerical dispatch. Prepared
+capture fields remain private and are not moved or exposed by this step.
+
+This new type/port-only library has no unit tests and declares `test=false` to
+avoid a new empty native harness. All existing consuming workflow and recovery
+behavior tests remain reachable. The overlay must be materialized and checked
+by the compiler, existing recovery/diagnostic/cancellation contracts, namespace
+and artifact inventories, and numerical callers after calibration. It is not
+an accepted routed or finalization extraction and is not ported to the refactor.
